# Every line carries an expiry (`CVE exp:YYYY-MM-DD`). On that date Trivy fails the release
# again, so the next Trino or base bump has to re-evaluate the finding rather than inherit
# the silence. Each line names the component, why nothing in a RunningLake deployment
# reaches it, and the fixed version. Measured 2026-09-24 with trivy 0.66.0 against the
# image built from this directory; Trino 483 is the newest release (published 2026-07-18),
# so none of these is fixable by upgrading.

# --- netty, inside the kept iceberg plugin (usr/lib/trino/plugin/iceberg) --------------
# SslClientHelloHandler is the SERVER side of TLS SNI routing: it selects an SslContext for
# an incoming ClientHello. Nothing in Trino runs a Netty TLS server — the HTTP server is
# Jetty — and the plugin uses Netty only as a client transport. Fixed in 4.2.17.Final.
CVE-2026-75595 exp:2026-12-31
# SCTP. Nothing in Trino opens an SCTP socket. Fixed in 4.2.17.Final.
CVE-2026-59902 exp:2026-12-31

# --- libthrift 0.23.0, inside the kept iceberg plugin -----------------------------------
# Reached only through an Iceberg catalog of type hive_metastore (a Thrift client to a
# metastore), and the loop needs a hostile SERVER response. RunningLake's Iceberg catalogs
# are REST (Lakekeeper); the image bakes no Thrift catalog, and the Hive and Hudi
# connectors are not shipped. Fixed in 0.24.0.
CVE-2026-43871 exp:2026-12-31

# --- the launcher, usr/lib/trino/bin/linux-amd64/launcher (Go 1.26.4, x/text 0.33.0) ---
# The launcher reads jvm.config, node.properties and launcher.properties — files baked
# into the image or mounted by the deployment, never input from a user or the network —
# and execs java. It serves no HTTP or HTTP/2, performs no TLS, and parses no DNS, XML,
# ASN.1, URLs, templates or untrusted text. Fixed in Go 1.26.6 / x/text 0.39.0; upstream
# rebuilds the launcher with each release, so the next Trino release is expected to clear
# these, and the expiry makes sure somebody looks.
CVE-2026-56852 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-12-31
